# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use TEM, a quantum function by Algorithmiq, to recover the dynamics of a 31-qubit kicked Ising chain from noisy hardware data, and compare it with PEC and ZNE."
msgstr "Pakai TEM, sebuah fungsi kuantum dari Algorithmiq, untuk memulihkan dinamika rantai kicked Ising 31-qubit dari data hardware yang noisy, dan bandingkan dengan PEC dan ZNE."

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Simulate a kicked Ising model with the TEM function"
msgstr "Simulasi model Ising terkick dengan fungsi TEM"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<OpenInLabBanner notebookPath=\"tutorials/simulate-kicked-ising-tem.ipynb\" />\n"
msgstr "<OpenInLabBanner notebookPath=\"tutorials/simulate-kicked-ising-tem.ipynb\" />\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "{/* cspell:ignore Floquet, linestyles, informationally */}\n"
msgstr "{/* cspell:ignore Floquet, linestyles, informationally */}\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Algorithmiq's Tensor-network Error Mitigation (TEM) method is a hybrid quantum-classical algorithm that removes the effect of hardware noise entirely in classical post-processing. The circuit runs on the QPU as written, with an informationally complete (IC) measurement at the end. A tensor network that inverts the learned noise of the device is then applied to the measurement outcomes, giving error-mitigated expectation values.\n"
msgstr "Metode Tensor-network Error Mitigation (TEM) dari Algorithmiq adalah algoritma hibrida kuantum-klasik yang menghilangkan efek noise hardware sepenuhnya dalam pasca-pemrosesan klasik. Circuit berjalan di QPU apa adanya, dengan pengukuran informationally complete (IC) di akhir. Tensor network yang menginvers noise perangkat yang dipelajari kemudian diterapkan pada hasil pengukuran, menghasilkan nilai ekspektasi yang sudah dimitigasi errornya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This tutorial reproduces, at 31 qubits, the kind of many-body dynamics experiment run on up to 91 qubits in [L. E. Fischer et al., Nat. Phys. (2026)](https://www.nature.com/articles/s41567-025-03144-9). It shows:\n"
msgstr "Tutorial ini mereproduksi, pada 31 qubit, jenis eksperimen dinamika many-body yang dijalankan hingga 91 qubit di [L. E. Fischer et al., Nat. Phys. (2026)](https://www.nature.com/articles/s41567-025-03144-9). Tutorial ini menunjukkan:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "How much signal hardware noise destroys in a utility-scale dynamics circuit, and how much TEM recovers.\n"
msgstr "Seberapa banyak sinyal yang dihancurkan noise hardware dalam circuit dinamika skala utilitas, dan seberapa banyak yang dipulihkan TEM.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "How TEM compares with probabilistic error cancellation (PEC) and zero-noise extrapolation (ZNE) on the same circuit.\n"
msgstr "Bagaimana TEM dibandingkan dengan probabilistic error cancellation (PEC) dan zero-noise extrapolation (ZNE) pada circuit yang sama.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The IC measurement also makes it possible to estimate observables that were not requested when the circuit ran, with a rerun of only the classical post-processing. For an example that estimates the full light cone of a chain, see [Run 4: measure the light cone from the same data](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/functions/algorithmiq-tem/performance-tuning#run-4-measure-the-light-cone-from-the-same-data).\n"
msgstr "Pengukuran IC juga memungkinkan estimasi observable yang tidak diminta saat circuit berjalan, dengan menjalankan ulang hanya pasca-pemrosesan klasik. Untuk contoh yang mengestimasi seluruh light cone sebuah rantai, lihat [Run 4: measure the light cone from the same data](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/functions/algorithmiq-tem/performance-tuning#run-4-measure-the-light-cone-from-the-same-data).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To tune TEM's accuracy against its QPU and classical cost, see the companion example [Tune the TEM function for accuracy and cost](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/functions/algorithmiq-tem/performance-tuning).\n"
msgstr "Untuk menyetel akurasi TEM terhadap biaya QPU dan klasiknya, lihat contoh pendamping [Tune the TEM function for accuracy and cost](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/functions/algorithmiq-tem/performance-tuning).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Usage estimate: approximately 20 QPU seconds for TEM on `ibm_phoenix` (the QPU time depends heavily on the chosen device). The optional PEC and ZNE comparison takes about 35 QPU minutes more, almost all of it for PEC.*\n"
msgstr "*Estimasi penggunaan: sekitar 20 detik QPU untuk TEM di `ibm_phoenix` (waktu QPU sangat bergantung pada perangkat yang dipilih). Perbandingan opsional PEC dan ZNE memakan sekitar 35 menit QPU lagi, hampir semuanya untuk PEC.*\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Background: the kicked Ising chain {#background-the-kicked-ising-chain}"
msgstr "Latar belakang: rantai kicked Ising {#background-the-kicked-ising-chain}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The kicked Ising model alternates an Ising evolution on a chain of $N$ qubits,\n"
msgstr "Model kicked Ising bergantian antara evolusi Ising pada rantai $N$ qubit,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$$ \\hat{H}_{\\text{I}} = J \\sum_{n=0}^{N-2} \\hat{Z}_n \\hat{Z}_{n+1} + h \\sum_{n=0}^{N-1} \\hat{Z}_n , $$\n"
msgstr "$$ \\hat{H}_{\\text{I}} = J \\sum_{n=0}^{N-2} \\hat{Z}_n \\hat{Z}_{n+1} + h \\sum_{n=0}^{N-1} \\hat{Z}_n , $$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "with a transverse kick,\n"
msgstr "dengan kick transversal,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$$ \\hat{H}_{K} = b \\sum_{n=0}^{N-1} \\hat{X}_n . $$\n"
msgstr "$$ \\hat{H}_{K} = b \\sum_{n=0}^{N-1} \\hat{X}_n . $$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "One period of the dynamics is the Floquet unitary $\\hat{U}_{\\text{KI}} = e^{-i \\hat{H}_K} e^{-i \\hat{H}_I}$. On a quantum computer each period is a brickwork of two-qubit $ZZ$ rotations followed by single-qubit rotations, so the circuit contains only two distinct layers of two-qubit gates, repeated.\n"
msgstr "Satu periode dinamika adalah unitary Floquet $\\hat{U}_{\\text{KI}} = e^{-i \\hat{H}_K} e^{-i \\hat{H}_I}$. Pada komputer kuantum, setiap periode adalah brickwork rotasi $ZZ$ dua-qubit diikuti rotasi satu-qubit, sehingga circuit hanya berisi dua layer Gate dua-qubit yang berbeda, yang diulang.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The quantity of interest is the infinite-temperature autocorrelation function of the first spin. The [reference paper](https://www.nature.com/articles/s41567-025-03144-9) shows that it can be measured by preparing the first qubit in $|+\\rangle$ and every other pair of qubits in the Bell state $(|00\\rangle + |11\\rangle)/\\sqrt{2}$, evolving for $t$ periods, and measuring a single-qubit Pauli operator $\\hat{X}_n$.\n"
msgstr "Besaran yang diminati adalah fungsi autokorelasi suhu-tak-hingga dari spin pertama. [Makalah acuan](https://www.nature.com/articles/s41567-025-03144-9) menunjukkan bahwa besaran ini bisa diukur dengan menyiapkan qubit pertama dalam $|+\\rangle$ dan setiap pasangan qubit lainnya dalam state Bell $(|00\\rangle + |11\\rangle)/\\sqrt{2}$, mengevolusikannya selama $t$ periode, dan mengukur operator Pauli satu-qubit $\\hat{X}_n$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "At the dual unitary point $|J| = |b| = \\pi/4$ the model is exactly solvable:\n"
msgstr "Pada titik dual unitary $|J| = |b| = \\pi/4$ model ini bisa diselesaikan secara eksak:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The correlation travels along the chain at maximal speed, so after $t$ periods only qubit $n = t$ carries it and $\\langle \\hat{X}_{n \\neq t} \\rangle = 0$.\n"
msgstr "Korelasi merambat sepanjang rantai dengan kecepatan maksimal, jadi setelah $t$ periode hanya qubit $n = t$ yang membawanya dan $\\langle \\hat{X}_{n \\neq t} \\rangle = 0$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "On that qubit, $\\langle \\hat{X}_{n=t} \\rangle = [\\cos(2h)]^t$.\n"
msgstr "Pada qubit tersebut, $\\langle \\hat{X}_{n=t} \\rangle = [\\cos(2h)]^t$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "These exact values make the model a sharp benchmark for error mitigation: the signal that reaches qubit $t$ has passed through every layer of the circuit, so it is exposed to all the noise of the device, yet its noiseless value is known. Away from the dual unitary point the same circuits become hard to simulate classically, which is where the paper uses TEM to go beyond exact methods.\n"
msgstr "Nilai-nilai eksak ini menjadikan model ini tolok ukur yang tajam untuk error mitigation: sinyal yang sampai ke qubit $t$ telah melewati setiap layer circuit, sehingga terpapar semua noise perangkat, namun nilai tanpa noise-nya diketahui. Di luar titik dual unitary, circuit yang sama menjadi sulit disimulasikan secara klasik, dan di situlah makalah tersebut memakai TEM untuk melampaui metode eksak.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "TEM works in three steps: it learns the noise of each distinct layer of two-qubit gates and the readout error, runs the circuit with an IC measurement, and finally applies the noise-inverting tensor network to the measurement outcomes on IBM Cloud&reg;.\n"
msgstr "TEM bekerja dalam tiga langkah: mempelajari noise setiap layer Gate dua-qubit yang berbeda dan error readout, menjalankan circuit dengan pengukuran IC, dan terakhir menerapkan tensor network penginvers noise pada hasil pengukuran di IBM Cloud&reg;.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setup {#setup}"
msgstr "Pengaturan {#setup}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "As a prerequisite, ensure that the necessary dependencies are installed.\n"
msgstr "Sebagai prasyarat, pastikan dependensi yang diperlukan sudah terinstal.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 1: Build the circuit and the observables {#step-1-build-the-circuit-and-the-observables}"
msgstr "Langkah 1: Bangun circuit dan observable {#step-1-build-the-circuit-and-the-observables}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This tutorial uses a circuit that implements the kicked Ising model described in the previous section. The circuit is prepared as follows. First, there is a state preparation phase, in which the first qubit is in the state $|+\\rangle$, while the others are in Bell pairs $(|00\\rangle + |11\\rangle)/\\sqrt{2}$. This is followed by the brickwork structure that implements the unitary evolution $\\hat{U}_{\\text{KI}}$. The number of physical time steps corresponds to $t/2$ circuit layers.\n"
"The following code builds the circuit used in this tutorial.\n"
msgstr ""
"Tutorial ini menggunakan sirkuit yang mengimplementasikan model Ising terkick yang dijelaskan di bagian sebelumnya. Sirkuit disiapkan sebagai berikut. Pertama, ada fase persiapan state, di mana qubit pertama berada dalam state $|+\\rangle$, sementara yang lain dalam pasangan Bell $(|00\\rangle + |11\\rangle)/\\sqrt{2}$. Ini diikuti oleh struktur brickwork yang mengimplementasikan evolusi unitary $\\hat{U}_{\\text{KI}}$. Jumlah langkah waktu fisik sesuai dengan $t/2$ layer sirkuit.\n"
"Kode berikut membangun sirkuit yang digunakan dalam tutorial ini.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next, build the observable, $\\hat{X}_{n=t}$. It is constructed as a simple Pauli string with the order matching the one used by Qiskit:\n"
msgstr "Selanjutnya, bangun observabel, $\\hat{X}_{n=t}$. Ini dibangun sebagai string Pauli sederhana dengan urutan yang sesuai dengan yang digunakan oleh Qiskit:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The experiment uses 31 qubits and 15 periods at $h = 0$, so the exact value of $\\langle \\hat{X}_{n=15} \\rangle$ is 1. This is a utility-scale circuit with 465 two-qubit gates: 15 that prepare the Bell pairs and 30 in each period. The signal that reaches qubit 15 passes through hundreds of them.\n"
msgstr "Eksperimen ini memakai 31 qubit dan 15 periode pada $h = 0$, jadi nilai eksak $\\langle \\hat{X}_{n=15} \\rangle$ adalah 1. Ini adalah circuit skala utilitas dengan 465 Gate dua-qubit: 15 untuk menyiapkan pasangan Bell dan 30 di setiap periode. Sinyal yang sampai ke qubit 15 melewati ratusan di antaranya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 2: Run TEM on the QPU {#step-2-run-tem-on-the-qpu}"
msgstr "Langkah 2: Jalankan TEM di QPU {#step-2-run-tem-on-the-qpu}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next, get access to the TEM function and select a backend from the available devices. This code assumes you've already [saved your account](/guides/functions-get-started#install-qiskit-functions-catalog-client) to your local environment.\n"
msgstr "Selanjutnya, dapatkan akses ke fungsi TEM dan pilih backend dari perangkat yang tersedia. Kode ini mengasumsikan kamu sudah [menyimpan akunmu](/guides/functions-get-started#install-qiskit-functions-catalog-client) ke lingkungan lokal.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Load the TEM function from the [IBM Quantum&reg; Functions Catalog](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/functions):\n"
msgstr "Muat fungsi TEM dari [IBM Quantum&reg; Functions Catalog](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/functions):\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Transpile the circuit for the chosen device once, and map the observable onto the qubits it was placed on. TEM accepts this instruction set architecture (ISA) circuit as it is, and the PEC and ZNE comparison in Step 3 uses the same circuit, so all methods run the same gates on the same qubits.\n"
msgstr "Transpile circuit untuk perangkat yang dipilih sekali saja, dan petakan observable ke qubit tempat circuit ditempatkan. TEM menerima circuit instruction set architecture (ISA) ini apa adanya, dan perbandingan PEC dan ZNE di Langkah 3 memakai circuit yang sama, jadi semua metode menjalankan Gate yang sama pada qubit yang sama.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The following options are based on the physics of the circuit:\n"
msgstr "Opsi berikut didasarkan pada fisika circuit:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**`max_layers_to_learn: 4`**: an upper bound on the number of distinct layers of two-qubit gates whose noise is learned. The brickwork has only two distinct layers, so only those two are learned.\n"
msgstr "**`max_layers_to_learn: 4`**: batas atas jumlah layer Gate dua-qubit berbeda yang noise-nya dipelajari. Brickwork hanya memiliki dua layer berbeda, jadi hanya keduanya yang dipelajari.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**`default_shots: 100_000`**: the number of shots of the IC measurement, which sets the statistical precision of the estimate.\n"
msgstr "**`default_shots: 100_000`**: jumlah shot pengukuran IC, yang menentukan presisi statistik estimasi.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**`tem_max_bond_dimension: 128`** and **`tem_compression_cutoff: 1e-14`**: a moderate bond dimension that keeps the classical post-processing fast at 31 qubits, with a small cutoff so that the bond dimension is not truncated further.\n"
msgstr "**`tem_max_bond_dimension: 128`** dan **`tem_compression_cutoff: 1e-14`**: dimensi bond yang moderat agar pasca-pemrosesan klasik tetap cepat pada 31 qubit, dengan cutoff kecil supaya dimensi bond tidak dipangkas lebih lanjut.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**`private: False`**: keeps the job results downloadable later. Set it to `True` for confidential circuits.\n"
msgstr "**`private: False`**: membuat hasil job tetap bisa diunduh nanti. Setel ke `True` untuk Circuit yang bersifat rahasia.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The [performance tuning example](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/functions/algorithmiq-tem/performance-tuning) explains each of these options in detail.\n"
msgstr "[Contoh penyetelan performa](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/functions/algorithmiq-tem/performance-tuning) menjelaskan setiap opsi ini secara rinci.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Calculate the function size that the job needs with the size calculator provided by IBM&reg;, and pass it to `tem.run` as `function_size`. The calculator maps the circuit onto the backend and returns `S`, `M`, or `L` without submitting anything; see [Function sizes](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/functions/algorithmiq-tem/get-started#function-sizes).\n"
msgstr "Hitung ukuran fungsi yang dibutuhkan job dengan kalkulator ukuran yang disediakan IBM&reg;, lalu teruskan ke `tem.run` sebagai `function_size`. Kalkulator ini memetakan Circuit ke Backend dan mengembalikan `S`, `M`, atau `L` tanpa mengirim apa pun; lihat [Function sizes](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/functions/algorithmiq-tem/get-started#function-sizes).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Finally, run the experiment, get the result, and visualize it. This step takes approximately 20 QPU seconds on `ibm_phoenix`.\n"
msgstr "Terakhir, jalankan eksperimen, dapatkan hasilnya, dan visualisasikan. Langkah ini membutuhkan sekitar 20 detik QPU di `ibm_phoenix`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Save the job ID. Use it to retrieve the results later with `catalog.get_job_by_id(job_id)`, or to rerun the post-processing.\n"
msgstr "Simpan ID job. Pakai ID itu untuk mengambil hasilnya nanti dengan `catalog.get_job_by_id(job_id)`, atau untuk menjalankan ulang pasca-pemrosesan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 3: Compare with PEC and ZNE {#step-3-compare-with-pec-and-zne}"
msgstr "Langkah 3: Bandingkan dengan PEC dan ZNE {#step-3-compare-with-pec-and-zne}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The result metadata also contains the unmitigated estimate, computed from the same measurement outcomes without the noise-inverting network. A comparison of the two with the exact value shows how much of the signal the noise destroys, and how much TEM recovers:\n"
"To put the TEM result in context, run the same circuit with two other error mitigation methods: probabilistic error cancellation (PEC) and zero-noise extrapolation (ZNE) with probabilistic error amplification (PEA).\n"
"<Admonition type=\"caution\">\n"
"  The following code runs a large PEC experiment, which requires around 40 minutes of QPU time.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"Metadata hasil juga berisi estimasi tanpa mitigasi, yang dihitung dari hasil pengukuran yang sama tanpa jaringan pembalik noise. Membandingkan keduanya dengan nilai eksak menunjukkan seberapa banyak sinyal yang dirusak noise, dan seberapa banyak yang dipulihkan TEM:\n"
"Untuk menempatkan hasil TEM dalam konteks, jalankan Circuit yang sama dengan dua metode mitigasi error lainnya: probabilistic error cancellation (PEC) dan zero-noise extrapolation (ZNE) dengan probabilistic error amplification (PEA).\n"
"<Admonition type=\"caution\">\n"
"  Kode berikut menjalankan eksperimen PEC besar, yang membutuhkan sekitar 40 menit waktu QPU.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "> **Note:** Each mitigation method can produce expectation values that are either higher or lower than the exact result. The standard deviations reflect statistical uncertainty only; they do not account for inaccuracies in the characterized noise model, because that model has no associated error bound.\n"
msgstr "> **Catatan:** Setiap metode mitigasi bisa menghasilkan nilai ekspektasi yang lebih tinggi atau lebih rendah dari hasil eksak. Deviasi standar hanya mencerminkan ketidakpastian statistik; deviasi itu tidak memperhitungkan ketidakakuratan model noise yang dikarakterisasi, karena model tersebut tidak punya batas error.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The unmitigated value decays with the number of noisy gates in the light cone of qubit 15, so at this depth most of the signal is lost. TEM removes this decay in post-processing, recovering most of the signal without running any additional circuits. The remaining gap to the exact value comes from the speed-oriented settings used in this tutorial: a bond dimension of 128 and a modest noise-learning budget. The [performance tuning example](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/functions/algorithmiq-tem/performance-tuning) shows how to trade QPU and classical time for accuracy.\n"
msgstr "Nilai tanpa mitigasi meluruh seiring jumlah Gate yang noisy di light cone qubit 15, jadi pada kedalaman ini sebagian besar sinyal hilang. TEM menghilangkan peluruhan ini lewat pasca-pemrosesan, memulihkan sebagian besar sinyal tanpa menjalankan Circuit tambahan. Selisih yang tersisa terhadap nilai eksak berasal dari pengaturan yang berorientasi kecepatan dalam tutorial ini: dimensi bond 128 dan anggaran noise-learning yang sederhana. [Contoh penyetelan performa](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/functions/algorithmiq-tem/performance-tuning) menunjukkan cara menukar waktu QPU dan waktu klasik demi akurasi.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next steps {#next-steps}"
msgstr "Langkah selanjutnya {#next-steps}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Change $h$ in the circuit to move away from the exact value $[\\cos(2h)]^t = 1$, or away from the dual unitary point, where classical simulation becomes hard. See [L. E. Fischer et al., Nat. Phys. (2026)](https://www.nature.com/articles/s41567-025-03144-9) for results up to 91 qubits.\n"
msgstr "Ubah $h$ di Circuit untuk menjauh dari nilai eksak $[\\cos(2h)]^t = 1$, atau menjauh dari titik dual unitary, tempat simulasi klasik menjadi sulit. Lihat [L. E. Fischer et al., Nat. Phys. (2026)](https://www.nature.com/articles/s41567-025-03144-9) untuk hasil hingga 91 qubit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Learn how each TEM option affects accuracy, QPU time, and classical time in [Tune the TEM function for accuracy and cost](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/functions/algorithmiq-tem/performance-tuning).\n"
msgstr "Pelajari bagaimana setiap opsi TEM memengaruhi akurasi, waktu QPU, dan waktu klasik di [Tune the TEM function for accuracy and cost](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/functions/algorithmiq-tem/performance-tuning).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "See the full list of options in the [TEM API reference](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/functions/algorithmiq-tem/api-reference).\n"
msgstr "Lihat daftar lengkap opsi di [referensi API TEM](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/functions/algorithmiq-tem/api-reference).\n"

#. type: Plain text
